    "question": {
      ":question/id": "03f27015-156e-5461-92a4-9680c924c621",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle {(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right))}^{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)+{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)+{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)]-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =1-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right))}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
