      ":question/id": "62e190f5-118c-597e-80ad-e7f3300ba1d6",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={105}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) & =4(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{210}^{∘} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})=-2.\n$$",
