      ":question/id": "82864e86-9a3e-5480-9b32-ad40c362a8c3",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$",
