      ":question/id": "6a60d369-36f7-5d41-afdf-2a280e580984",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle {(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right))}^{2}.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right))}^{2}=\n$$\n{{value}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we expand the parentheses and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)+{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)+{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)]+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right))}^{2}=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$",
