      ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}=\n$$\n{{value}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\\right)}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$",
